(import :clan/poo/object)
(export DesignReadings)
(def DesignReadings (.o inspections: (list
(.o identity: 'curiosity-reading-9cfb68af1eb9 view: 'policy-generation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-fdb547310b037c5134b2652ed5c16242c434e0b11f2837e793229d4775509745 image-sha: "9cfb68af1eb985e13e0d845b1a3e7741f4c99211482908bb416942529b44a1ac" question: 'why-refuse producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the final exported PNG. My initial guess from the title would be that matching policy words should let the update proceed. The fork gives me a visible way to test that guess: Record at capture / version tag / 7 branches to Owner record now / version tag / 8 and Request saved / version tag / 7. The same paper strokes remain while the live tag changes; the snapshot frame keeps the request's old tag. At the lens, Owner now / version tag / 8 meets Request saved / version tag / 7. The equal policy strokes and different neutral tags supply the surprising clue: this is an identity match, not a larger-is-better judgment. I can now ask why matching words cannot rescue a stale expectation, and what would change if the saved tag matched the live tag. That experiment would remove this mismatch, not prove all admission conditions. The horizontal arm visibly stops the attempted update; the separate receipt and No update. Refusal saved. caption show the consequence without replacing the live record. The balanced fork lets me follow both branches into the check without a long corner tail. Lens labels are clear of the rim, captions fit, scoped text remains above 18 px, and routes remain under the unchanged detour bound. The snapshot is an explanatory metaphor for the frozen expected generation and digest, not a literal claim that all policy bytes are copied. This is a new unapplied request, not the historical ACK of an already-applied retry. The picture offers a concrete discrepancy to investigate and a counterfactual to ask; this is my located model reading, not evidence that a particular child felt curiosity or understood the design. Keep the six Explore questions open rather than recording an engagement pass.")
(.o identity: 'curiosity-reading-7bc5fb122e17 view: 'policy-generation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-fdb547310b037c5134b2652ed5c16242c434e0b11f2837e793229d4775509745 image-sha: "7bc5fb122e17798f2944e615590d3478b77fe773cd70ef6b2a606e2abf8024b6" question: 'why-refuse producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the balanced third PNG. I first see one saved record branching into an updated live version tag 8 and a retained request tag 7. The two paths meet at the lens, so the challenge is now to discover which part differs although the policy strokes match. The tag labels name the field and its role without a higher-is-better color cue. The horizontal stop arm visibly blocks the attempted motion and the receipt is a separate saved consequence. Text is above the unchanged reader target. I would investigate whether keeping the same policy text can rescue a request whose saved tag differs, and then ask what a matching tag would change: it removes this mismatch, not the other admission checks. The module still reports a measurable input-route detour (302.46 versus 145.31 px). Give the causal neighborhood a clearer incoming approach, without lowering the route threshold. These are located visual findings and open inquiry, not a young-reader-understood verdict.")
(.o identity: 'curiosity-reading-08d983b31aaa view: 'policy-generation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-fdb547310b037c5134b2652ed5c16242c434e0b11f2837e793229d4775509745 image-sha: "08d983b31aaa340c5a46837e019e496ab49c5469ef3a1306e07119417d5acd70" question: 'why-refuse producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the second exported PNG. The lowered horizontal arm now stops the attempted upward motion, and the lens no longer crosses the version-tag labels. Version tag is locally named on every number, so no arithmetic ranking or unexplained generation term is required. But the native compound group still lays out in the global rightward direction: its child DOWN preference does not create a vertical neighborhood with cross-hierarchy edges. The consequence remains stranded at the lower right. The minimum scoped font is still 17.90 px. Use the solver's balanced split/rejoin placement for this inferred causal fork and shorten redundant relation wording. Keep the open question: matching words versus a stale saved tag. Do not interpret these observations as evidence that a learner is engaged.")
(.o identity: 'curiosity-reading-0d6b32274dd4 view: 'policy-generation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-fdb547310b037c5134b2652ed5c16242c434e0b11f2837e793229d4775509745 image-sha: "0d6b32274dd4951b5ea768916cd98fda3dd5893abcf9bc93a57248c1f37b2428" question: 'why-refuse producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the actual exported PNG. The split from one record into a turning live record and a retained snapshot gives me something to follow. The inspection lens invites me to compare the two tags rather than read five abstract boxes. But its rim crosses the generation labels. Generation is still unexplained vocabulary for a young novice. More seriously the barrier is raised: it visually suggests passage while STOP and REFUSED claim refusal. The consequence must depict the attempted motion actually stopped. The check and consequence occupy a long rightward tail leaving the upper-right area empty, and the rightmost caption reaches the edge. The scoped minimum text is 17.93 px. Keep the causal fork, organize check and its immediate consequence as a compact neighborhood, show the stop action consistently, and use version tag as the local property name. The question I can investigate is why matching text does not save the old expectation; these observations do not establish a child's interest or understanding.")
(.o identity: 'reader-interest-rejection-2334865edc7d view: 'policy-generation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-fdb547310b037c5134b2652ed5c16242c434e0b11f2837e793229d4775509745 image-sha: "2334865edc7d22a240f4c47d8f96569cff48336e8675328af393618dd840ac26" question: 'why-refuse producer: 'current-model response: "The user actually read this image and could not understand what it communicates. It feels neither vivid nor engaging and consists of boxes. The elementary-school perspective means a learner's curiosity and willingness to explore, not a child character or merely simpler vocabulary. Re-viewing the PNG, I agree: static labeled records make text do the explanatory work, while capture, change, an expectation remaining behind, and the reason for refusal are not perceptible actions. Source binding, number labels, font size and zero requests did not establish an effective explanation. Reopen the representation and let the model reason about an engaging, faithful visual mechanism rather than filling the existing boxes.")
(.o identity: 'meaning-reading-2334865edc7d view: 'policy-generation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-fdb547310b037c5134b2652ed5c16242c434e0b11f2837e793229d4775509745 image-sha: "2334865edc7d22a240f4c47d8f96569cff48336e8675328af393618dd840ac26" question: 'why-refuse producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the actual PNG and independently displayed SVG. The number 8 is now inside the record labeled Owner record now, directly under generation; it identifies the owner's current registered head after the deadline event. It is not a permission or quality score. The earlier record and the request each explicitly retain generation 7. In the check, Owner now / generation / 8 is compared with Request saved / generation / 7. These are record references requiring exact equality, not a ranking or an argument that a larger number wins. The shared policy text is explicitly named, without X. Both owner records use the same neutral visual encoding. The envelope preserves a captured expectation, and the refusal receipt records no update while keeping the current record. This example says the request has not yet been applied; it does not conflate new admission with historical acknowledgement of a completed retry. This records the meanings and relationships I can point to, not a learner-understood verdict.")
(.o identity: 'meaning-clear-spacing-open view: 'policy-generation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-fdb547310b037c5134b2652ed5c16242c434e0b11f2837e793229d4775509745 image-sha: "feaefbb08cf27426e9f632e1f1a49a349015b51defea8e66d62805a9a451dbc8" question: 'why-refuse producer: 'current-model response: "The meanings and operational uses of all five generation values are now locally identifiable and were cited from the actual PNG/SVG. ASCENT nevertheless retains three relayout requests because each record's role label and generation label have intersecting measured text rectangles. The semantic reading must not overrule that geometry. Increase spacing within the local record/request illustrations while keeping their role, property, value and exact-match use unchanged.")
(.o identity: 'meaning-reading-feaefbb08cf2 view: 'policy-generation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-fdb547310b037c5134b2652ed5c16242c434e0b11f2837e793229d4775509745 image-sha: "feaefbb08cf27426e9f632e1f1a49a349015b51defea8e66d62805a9a451dbc8" question: 'why-refuse producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the actual PNG and independently displayed SVG. The number 8 is now inside the record labeled Owner record now, directly under generation; it identifies the owner's current registered head after the deadline event. It is not a permission or quality score. The earlier record and the request each explicitly retain generation 7. In the check, Owner now / generation / 8 is compared with Request saved / generation / 7. These are record references requiring exact equality, not a ranking or an argument that a larger number wins. The shared policy text is explicitly named, without X. Both owner records use the same neutral visual encoding. The envelope preserves a captured expectation, and the refusal receipt records no update while keeping the current record. This example says the request has not yet been applied; it does not conflate new admission with historical acknowledgement of a completed retry. This records the meanings and relationships I can point to, not a learner-understood verdict.")
(.o identity: 'locally-bound-number-reading view: 'policy-generation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-fdb547310b037c5134b2652ed5c16242c434e0b11f2837e793229d4775509745 image-sha: "23eb7e152bccf7917e9aa43376c7253ba3e84d3b378d70a956e4f1e4e88cc3e7" question: 'why-refuse producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the new PNG. Each generation now has a local record role, property name and value, with neutral colors rather than a green higher-number implication. In the check, Owner now / generation / 8 and Request saved / generation / 7 name the two references directly. The image no longer relies on X or a large arithmetic inequality. However, explanatory captions and edge labels repeat information already inside the objects and reduce scoped body text to about 17 px. Remove that redundancy without deleting the local meanings. Also state that this is a request not yet applied, so the illustration does not conflate stale new admission with historical acknowledgement of an already-applied retry.")
(.o identity: 'user-symbol-meaning-reading view: 'policy-generation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-fdb547310b037c5134b2652ed5c16242c434e0b11f2837e793229d4775509745 image-sha: "1fb429410844fd77613dd008915c4fde1400542e84303f98a0e26ed2f0527f6a" question: 'why-refuse producer: 'current-model response: "The user's actual image reading identifies a failure that font and route metrics missed. Bare 7, 8 and X make the reader infer what record each value belongs to and why it matters. The large unequal numbers can be mistaken for an arithmetic or ranking argument; orange versus green may suggest a better or authorized state. Generation 7 denotes the registered head captured by the request; generation 8 denotes the owner's current registered head. Admission requires an exact match, not a larger value. Bind every shown value locally to its role and quantity, keep identity encodings neutral, and remove the unexplained X placeholder.")
(.o identity: 'third-policy-reading view: 'policy-generation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-fdb547310b037c5134b2652ed5c16242c434e0b11f2837e793229d4775509745 image-sha: "79150ba23fb1d1c69c5ccb7b1b3b4a066c55377da75c5f88c11923ac1682ca4e" question: 'why-refuse producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the owner-counter version. Its meaning now distinguishes the unchanged policy content from the changed owner generation. The Module independently reports reader-text-too-small on six scoped captions: the actual size is 17.27 px, below its unchanged 18 px reader target. The longer single-line deadline relation consumes horizontal space. Keep all source conditions and shorten the relation wording, instead of lowering the reader target or supplying a favorable verdict.")
(.o identity: 'second-policy-reading view: 'policy-generation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-fdb547310b037c5134b2652ed5c16242c434e0b11f2837e793229d4775509745 image-sha: "d6033b73e121d06fa0f472773ff9e9eded5fbbf90edcb2eaa43f723e70a86778" question: 'why-refuse producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the second PNG. Its numbers, frozen expectation and refusal are easier to follow, and its measured minimum text is 18.42 px. However, revision can mean the immutable policy revision rather than the owner's registered generation. Calling these the same would obscure the very reason for checking unchanged content. Name the changing quantity as the owner's version counter and leave content X unchanged. The request and the current counter must still meet at the comparison.")
(.o identity: 'first-policy-reading view: 'policy-generation revision: 'design source-cut: 'sha256-fdb547310b037c5134b2652ed5c16242c434e0b11f2837e793229d4775509745 image-sha: "1a23f4fe1c506286d0ac978121548d878f0a21c20ff3446630e48be984153dda" question: 'why-refuse producer: 'current-model response: "I viewed the actual PNG. The envelope retains 7 while the current policy shows 8 and the comparison visibly rejects it. However, generation, policy head and bytes presume vocabulary I have not explained to a beginner. The smallest text is about 15 px and long edge captions consume width. Explain generation as the owner's revision number, content X as unchanged content, and shorten relational wording while keeping the actual source conditions. The same document shape across 7 and 8 helps me compare what changes and what stays.")
) image-evidence: (list
